  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia-Papua New Guinea Economic Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia Papua New Guinea Economic Partnership (APEP) is the main vehicle and coordination point from which Australia delivers its economic development support to Papua New Guinea (PNG). APEP is focused on supporting PNG&#x2019;s efforts to achieve sustained economic growth, capable of lifting the standard of living of all citizens, with a focus on supporting macroeconomic stability, public financial management reforms, and inclusive growth through livelihood initiatives in the agricultural sector and small-to-medium enterprise (SME) development. Additional programs also support PNG&#x2019;s biosecurity standards for trade and market access, and policy support on food security.</narrative>
  </description>
